; Pin a Dirichlet vector via `dirichlet_eq`, then query a downstream
; categorical drawn from the same vector. The categorical's posterior should
; match the pinned vector's components exactly: P(c=0)=0.2, P(c=1)=0.8.
; Exercises the `Pinned` Dirichlet prior flowing through a categorical
; (the `Counts × Pinned` posterior path).
(query
  (let ((p (dirichlet 1.0 1.0))
        (c (categorical p)))
    (Posterior c (dirichlet_eq p {0.2, 0.8}))))
